      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Two pointers - merge from the ends</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/squares-of-a-sorted-array/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 977</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Squares of a Sorted Array</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Squaring breaks the order only for the negatives, and the largest square left is always at one of the two ends. Put a pointer at each end, write the bigger square into the last free slot, move that pointer inward. O(n) time instead of the O(n log n) \"square then sort\". Uber and Meta ask it as a warm-up and then push on the follow-up: what if the transform is a general quadratic?</p>\n"
  },
